########################################################################

DOCUMENT();      

loadMacros(
   "PGstandard.pl",     # Standard macros for PG language
   "MathObjects.pl",
   #"source.pl",        # allows code to be displayed on certain sites.
   #"PGcourse.pl",      # Customization file for the course
);

# Print problem number and point value (weight) for the problem
TEXT(beginproblem());

# Show which answers are correct and which ones are incorrect
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

##############################################################
#
#  Setup
#
#
Context("Numeric");

$q1 = Compute("pi"); #M4 Q7 a)
$q2 = Compute("pi"); #M4 Q7 b)
$q3 = Compute("pi"); #M4 Q7 c)



##############################################################
#
#  Text
#
#

Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT
Let \( F(x,y,z) = (x-y,y+z,3z-2). \) Here are three surfaces all oriented with \( \textbf{upward} \) unit normal. $BR

a) Disk \( D  = \lbrace (x,y,z) \in \mathbb{R}^3 : x^2+y^2\leq 1, z=0 \rbrace \) $BR
b) Paraboloid \( P  = \lbrace (x,y,z) \in \mathbb{R}^3 : x^2+y^2\leq 1, z=1-x^2-y^2 \rbrace \) $BR
c) Hemisphere \( H  = \lbrace (x,y,z) \in \mathbb{R}^3 : x^2+y^2 +z^2 = 1, z \geq 0 \rbrace \) $BR
Find the total circulation of \( F \) over each surface. You may give an exact answer or round to two decimal places. \( \textit{Hint:} \) This is a three-for-one! 
$BR
a) \{$q1->ans_rule\}
$BR 
b) \{$q2->ans_rule\}
$BR 
c) \{$q3->ans_rule\}

END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;

##############################################################
#
#  Answers
#
#

ANS($q1->with(tolerance=>.01)->cmp);
ANS($q2->with(tolerance=>.01)->cmp);
ANS($q3->with(tolerance=>.01)->cmp);

# default tolerance is .01 or one percent.


ENDDOCUMENT();       